 "0001": {
  "title": "",
  "nodes": [
   {
    "id": "h4_00001",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     11
    ],
    "text": "[A1][/A1]NAME",
    "placeholders": {
     "A1": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_89_01\" id=\"tag_17_89_01\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "blockquote_00002",
    "type": "blockquote",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     13
    ],
    "text": "connect — connect a socket",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00003",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     15
    ],
    "text": "[A2][/A2]SYNOPSIS",
    "placeholders": {
     "A2": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_89_02\" id=\"tag_17_89_02\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00004",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     17,
     1
    ],
    "text": "[CODE3]",
    "placeholders": {
     "CODE3": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<code><tt>#include &lt;<a href=\"../basedefs/sys_socket.h.html\">sys/socket.h</a>&gt;<br>\n<br>\nint connect(int</tt> <i>socket</i><tt>, const struct sockaddr *</tt><i>address</i><tt>,<br>\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; socklen_t</tt> <i>address_len</i><tt>);<br></tt></code>"
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00005",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     19
    ],
    "text": "[A4][/A4]DESCRIPTION",
    "placeholders": {
     "A4": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_89_03\" id=\"tag_17_89_03\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00006",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     21,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The [I5]connect[/I5]() function shall attempt to make a connection on a connection-mode socket or to set or reset the peer address\nof a connectionless-mode socket. The function takes the following arguments:",
    "placeholders": {
     "I5": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00007",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     21,
     3,
     3
    ],
    "text": "[I6]socket[/I6]",
    "placeholders": {
     "I6": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00008",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     21,
     3,
     5
    ],
    "text": "Specifies the file descriptor associated with the socket.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00009",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     21,
     3,
     7
    ],
    "text": "[I7]address[/I7]",
    "placeholders": {
     "I7": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00010",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     21,
     3,
     9
    ],
    "text": "Points to a [B8]sockaddr[/B8] structure containing the peer address. The length and format of the address depend on the address\nfamily of the socket.",
    "placeholders": {
     "B8": {
      "open": "<b>",
      "close": "</b>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00011",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     21,
     3,
     11
    ],
    "text": "[I9]address_len[/I9]",
    "placeholders": {
     "I9": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00012",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     21,
     3,
     13
    ],
    "text": "Specifies the length of the [B10]sockaddr[/B10] structure pointed to by the [I11]address[/I11] argument.",
    "placeholders": {
     "B10": {
      "open": "<b>",
      "close": "</b>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I11": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00013",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     21,
     5
    ],
    "text": "If the address family of the socket is AF_UNIX, the application shall ensure that a null terminator after the pathname is\nincluded in the [I12]sun_path[/I12] member of [I13]address[/I13] as a [B14]sockaddr_un[/B14] structure, and that [I15]address_len[/I15] is at least\n[CODE16] plus the length of the pathname.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I12": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I13": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "B14": {
      "open": "<b>",
      "close": "</b>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I15": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "CODE16": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<tt>offsetof(struct sockaddr_un, sun_path) + 1</tt>"
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00014",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     21,
     7
    ],
    "text": "If the socket has not already been bound to a local address, [I17]connect[/I17]() shall bind it to an address which, unless the\nsocket's address family is AF_UNIX, is an unused local address.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I17": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00015",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     21,
     9
    ],
    "text": "If the initiating socket is not connection-mode, then [I18]connect[/I18]() shall set the socket's peer address, and no connection is\nmade. For SOCK_DGRAM sockets, the peer address identifies where all datagrams are sent on subsequent [A19][I20]send[/I20]()[/A19] functions, and limits the remote sender for subsequent [A21][I22]recv[/I22]()[/A21] functions. If the [I23]sa_family[/I23] member of [I24]address[/I24] is AF_UNSPEC, the socket's\npeer address shall be reset. Note that despite no connection being made, the term &quot;connected&quot; is used to describe a\nconnectionless-mode socket for which a peer address has been set.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I18": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A19": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/send.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I20": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A21": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/recv.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I22": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I23": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I24": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00016",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     21,
     11
    ],
    "text": "If the initiating socket is connection-mode, then [I25]connect[/I25]() shall attempt to establish a connection to the address\nspecified by the [I26]address[/I26] argument. If the connection cannot be established immediately and O_NONBLOCK is not set for the\nfile descriptor for the socket, [I27]connect[/I27]() shall block for up to an unspecified timeout interval until the connection is\nestablished. If the timeout interval expires before the connection is established, [I28]connect[/I28]() shall fail and the connection\nattempt shall be aborted. If [I29]connect[/I29]() is interrupted by a signal that is caught while blocked waiting to establish a\nconnection, [I30]connect[/I30]() shall fail and set [I31]errno[/I31] to [EINTR], but the connection request shall not be aborted, and the\nconnection shall be established asynchronously.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I25": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I26": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I27": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I28": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I29": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I30": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I31": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00017",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     21,
     13
    ],
    "text": "If the connection cannot be established immediately and O_NONBLOCK is set for the file descriptor for the socket,\n[I32]connect[/I32]() shall fail and set [I33]errno[/I33] to [EINPROGRESS], but the connection request shall not be aborted, and the\nconnection shall be established asynchronously. Subsequent calls to [I34]connect[/I34]() for the same socket, before the connection is\nestablished, shall fail and set [I35]errno[/I35] to [EALREADY].",
    "placeholders": {
     "I32": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I33": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I34": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I35": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00018",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     21,
     15
    ],
    "text": "When the connection has been established asynchronously, [A36][I37]pselect[/I37]()[/A36], [A38][I39]select[/I39]()[/A38], [A40][I41]poll[/I41]()[/A40], and [A42][I43]ppoll[/I43]()[/A42] shall indicate that the file descriptor for the socket is ready for writing.",
    "placeholders": {
     "A36": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/pselect.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I37": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A38": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/select.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I39": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A40": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/poll.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I41": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A42": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/ppoll.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I43": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00019",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     21,
     17
    ],
    "text": "The socket in use may require the process to have appropriate privileges to use the [I44]connect[/I44]() function.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I44": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00020",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     23
    ],
    "text": "[A45][/A45]RETURN VALUE",
    "placeholders": {
     "A45": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_89_04\" id=\"tag_17_89_04\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00021",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     25,
     1
    ],
    "text": "Upon successful completion, [I46]connect[/I46]() shall return 0; otherwise, -1 shall be returned and [I47]errno[/I47] set to indicate\nthe error.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I46": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I47": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00022",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     27
    ],
    "text": "[A48][/A48]ERRORS",
    "placeholders": {
     "A48": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_89_05\" id=\"tag_17_89_05\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00023",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The [I49]connect[/I49]() function shall fail if:",
    "placeholders": {
     "I49": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00024",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     3
    ],
    "text": "[EADDRNOTAVAIL]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00025",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     5
    ],
    "text": "The specified address is not available from the local machine.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00026",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     7
    ],
    "text": "[EAFNOSUPPORT]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00027",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     9
    ],
    "text": "The specified address is not a valid address for the address family of the specified socket.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00028",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     11
    ],
    "text": "[EALREADY]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00029",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     13
    ],
    "text": "A connection request is already in progress for the specified socket.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00030",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     15
    ],
    "text": "[EBADF]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00031",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     17
    ],
    "text": "The [I50]socket[/I50] argument is not a valid file descriptor.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I50": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00032",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     19
    ],
    "text": "[ECONNREFUSED]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00033",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     21
    ],
    "text": "The target address was not listening for connections or refused the connection request.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00034",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     23
    ],
    "text": "[EINPROGRESS]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00035",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     25
    ],
    "text": "O_NONBLOCK is set for the file descriptor for the socket and the connection cannot be immediately established; the connection\nshall be established asynchronously.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00036",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     27
    ],
    "text": "[EINTR]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00037",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     29
    ],
    "text": "The attempt to establish a connection was interrupted by delivery of a signal that was caught; the connection shall be\nestablished asynchronously.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00038",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     31
    ],
    "text": "[EISCONN]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00039",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     33
    ],
    "text": "The specified socket is connection-mode and is already connected.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00040",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     35
    ],
    "text": "[ENETUNREACH]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00041",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     37
    ],
    "text": "No route to the network is present.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
