   {
    "id": "p_00084",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     41,
     3
    ],
    "text": "For AF_UNIX sockets, some implementations support an extension where [I63]address_len[/I63] does not have to include a null\nterminator for the pathname stored in [I64]sun_path[/I64], which in turn allows a pathname to be one byte longer. However, such usage\nis not portable, and carries a risk of accessing beyond the intended bounds of the pathname length.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I63": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I64": {
